  "scope": "Both shared ImGui launchers submit histogram Calculate/Replay to native workers, display stage progress/cancellation and publish detached results/defaults/workflow only on the creator thread.",
  "semantics": "The application shared scheduler owns work. Commands, limits and recording choice are captured at submission. Duplicate processing is refused; pending inputs are disabled while old results remain exportable. Cancel/close, source data/selection/closure, native activation and draft changes cancel or discard work. Same-dataset navigation preserves captured planes. Queued cancellation retires immediately; running cancellation is cooperative. Both launchers use the target accumulator for simple and scientific modes, so nonconstant raw UInt16/Float32 simple calculations now use two source passes.",
  "publication": "The creator polls READY results, stages owned DTO/bin/statistic/record copies, revalidates source/draft, reserves the captured workflow entry and saves defaults before non-throwing result ownership moves. Replay does not save defaults. Preference-save and workflow-array refusal preserve prior result/defaults/workflow. Completion updates only result fields, preserving presentation changes such as closing Target while queued. Explicit-position result captions no longer assume a range target.",
  "api": "calculate_histogram and replay_histogram submit asynchronously. poll/wait/wait_jobs or wait_histogram observe completion; wait_histogram validates timeout_ms in 1..60000 (default5000) and propagates publication errors. cancel_histogram accepts no parameters. Existing Python active_index busy guard is retained; native activation changes cancel jobs, including activation ABA. Generic cancel_job and thread-safe Window.cancel also reach histogram tickets.",
  "verification": "1527 selected checks per OS including 31 new API/input checks; ten native executable suites, including twelve native Window scenarios for blocked queues, cancellation, source/draft/activation/closure, captured recording, preference/workflow refusal and readonly history. Independent readers verify 232 reports / 31133 input frames, including 24 new async reports / 1700 frames. New real inputs prove queued cancellation, stale source/draft handling, closure, replay after navigation and preserving a closed Target dialog. No complete upstream reference/resource/real-GPU/platform acceptance.",
